From 7b7d8c897a4f48b33ffe21189354cc429ada5585 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 11:37:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] v4.6-gpu: GPU virtual time scheduling, cross-scheduler
 coupling, KERNEL vtime boost

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>

v4.6-gpu: fix 4 bugs from RiverOnVenus review and redesign kernel.infinity_stats

Fixes identified by RiverOnVenus (github issue #15):

1. UAF on infinity_entity pointer (CRITICAL):
   Move cleanup in drm_sched_entity_kill() to AFTER wait_for_completion
   so that all in-flight jobs are guaranteed to be in pending_list
   before scanning.  Also scan ALL schedulers in the entity's
   sched_list (multi-scheduler safety).

2. Lock domain doc mismatch (MEDIUM):
   Update gpu_time_ema, gpu_time_total, gpu_time_last_active kernel-doc
   to say 'Written under sched->job_list_lock on completion; read under
   rq->lock during scheduling' instead of the incorrect 'Protected by
   rq->lock.'

3. Silent accounting loss via spin_trylock (HIGH):
   Defer GPU time accounting from drm_sched_job_done() (fence callback,
   IRQ context) to drm_sched_get_finished_job() (free worker, process
   context).  Job done now only does WRITE_ONCE(infinity_gpu_ns) +
   atomic_inc(completion_callbacks).  get_finished_job reads the
   saved entity + gpu_ns under job_list_lock (full spin_lock, no
   trylock).  Accounting is always applied or counted as skipped.

4. Misleading stats counters (MEDIUM):
   Split GPU counter into completion_callbacks, accounting_applied, and
   accounting_skipped so users can verify cb == app + skipped.
   Remove phantom 'Sleep decays' line (was same counter as EMA climbs),
   remove redundant 'EMA updates' line (was identical to jobs_completed),
   remove reductive 'Health' section.  Add real infinity_wakeup_count
   incremented in infinity_wakeup().

Stats redesign:
   Match the agreed format from the mockup: raw comma-formatted numbers
   aligned in 14-char columns, Unicode box-drawing for tree breakdown,
   sections for CPU/RT/GPU, Accounting confidence line with percentage,
   and Verdict.  Counter reads go through '(unsigned int)' cast to
   prevent sign-extension of wrapped 32-bit atomic_t values.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
